public import Theory.Representation.Mathieu.SmallModules.M12Recognition.PointClassification.NormalizedInvolution.NormIdeal
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin

/-!
# Candidate coordinates for the M₁₁ eleven-norm quotient

The 300 words and two packed matrices are witness data from exact binary
elimination, using the literal Atlas generators. Columns describe proposed
LEFT multiplication by A and B, with bit zero the first coordinate. The words
are evaluated in the actual group, never in a group defined by a presentation.

This module defines the common input for two independent certificates:
normal-form lifting modulo `elevenIdeal`, and a three-step filtration with
augmentation-module factors. No quotient identity or nilpotence assertion is
made here. See `source/README.md` for the contracts and reproduction command.
Source application: Aschbacher–Smith G.7.3(2), printed p.348/PDF p.359,
citing James, J. Algebra 27 (1973), 57–111.
-/

@[expose] public section
open scoped MonoidAlgebra
namespace Representation.MathieuSmall.M12Recognition.PointClassification.NormalizedInvolution.CertificateData
open Sporadic.Mathieu

abbrev Space := Fin 300 → ZMod 2

/-- The actual marked generators, in the order A, B. -/
noncomputable def generator (s : Fin 2) : M11 :=
  if s = 0 then m11GeneratorAInM11 else m11GeneratorBInM11

/-- Evaluate from left to right using multiplication by function composition. -/
noncomputable def evalWord (w : List (Fin 2)) : M11 := (w.map generator).prod

